[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3801918608","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115406#issuecomment-3801918608","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115406","id":3801918608,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7inKyQ","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T21:48:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T06:07:35Z","body":"I can reproduce it on macOS 26 (with built-in VoiceOver), and Fedora 43 (with Orca and both X11 and Wayland display server on Wayland session).\n\n_Edit: Missed toggling screen reader on-off-on, and only tested enabling it before and after launch, will recheck later._","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3801918608/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3804059725","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115406#issuecomment-3804059725","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115406","id":3804059725,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ivVhN","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T09:22:18Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T09:22:18Z","body":"> Edit: Missed toggling screen reader on-off-on, and only tested enabling it before and after launch, will recheck later.\n\nRechecked with toggling screen reader on-off-on, and it is reproducible on Linux. But not on Windows (NVDA) or macOS (VoiceOver). Likely accesskit is loosing existing tree information when screen reader is disabled on Linux, but not on other platforms.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3804059725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813352620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115406#issuecomment-3813352620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115406","id":3813352620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jSySs","user":{"login":"DataTriny","id":11966864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTY2ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11966864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny","html_url":"https://github.com/DataTriny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DataTriny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T19:12:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T19:12:17Z","body":"@bruvzg The reason why this bug only shows up on Linux is because this is the only platform on which we can detect when to disable an AccessKit adapter. It was previously \"hidden\" because we were activating/deactivating based on whether accessibility was enabled on the system (something that typically doesn't change once a session is open but not when you start or stop an assistive technology). Now that we track whether an AT is running, `AccessibilityDriverAccessKit::_accessibility_initial_tree_update_callback` can be called multiple times and you need to send the whole tree every time. Since you're only sending a window node in here, I suppose that the next tree update that is pushed only contain a diff to the tree update that was pushed before `AccessibilityDriverAccessKit::_accessibility_deactivation_callback` was invoked. When we deactivate an adapter, we forget its state in order to save resource, so we basically restart fresh.\n\nHope this helps.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813352620/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813537194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115406#issuecomment-3813537194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115406","id":3813537194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jTfWq","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T19:50:21Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T19:50:21Z","body":"> AccessibilityDriverAccessKit::_accessibility_initial_tree_update_callback can be called multiple times and you need to send the whole tree every time. Since you're only sending a window node in here\n\nYes, this definitely was not accounted for, and we indeed send only changes.","author_association":"MEMBER","p